WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:20.147
"Get these dinosaurs out of here!" cried Professor Flashback.

2
00:00:20.148 --> 00:00:24.623
Several dinosaurs jumped onto a table and knocked over equipment.

3
00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:27.483
A small clock fell down and broke.

4
00:00:27.484 --> 00:00:30.772
Another dinosaur ate books from the bookshelf.

5
00:00:30.773 --> 00:00:33.759
"They're destroying my laboratory!"

6
00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:36.460
Professor Flashback pulled at his hair.

7
00:00:36.461 --> 00:00:39.799
Roxy saw a big dinosaur bump into the big clock.

8
00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:41.792
The clock rocked.

9
00:00:41.793 --> 00:00:43.520
Roxy gulped.

10
00:00:43.521 --> 00:00:48.474
"If that clock breaks, Metro City will be trapped in the past!"

11
00:00:48.475 --> 00:00:51.011
She darted to the clock and grabbed it.

12
00:00:51.012 --> 00:00:56.564
The clock's big hand was pointing to the year 65 million BC.

13
00:00:56.565 --> 00:00:59.510
"Shoo!" said Professor Flashback.

14
00:00:59.511 --> 00:01:03.037
He was pushing three small dinosaurs away with a broom.

15
00:01:03.038 --> 00:01:05.942
He suddenly spotted Roxy near the clock.

16
00:01:05.943 --> 00:01:08.596
"What are you doing?" he yelled.

17
00:01:08.597 --> 00:01:10.106
Roxy glared at him.

18
00:01:10.107 --> 00:01:13.754
"I'm bringing Metro City back to the present!"

19
00:01:13.755 --> 00:01:16.049
She grabbed the clock's hand.

20
00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:21.158
"No!" cried Professor Flashback. "Do not—oof!"

21
00:01:21.159 --> 00:01:24.047
A fat dinosaur knocked the professor down.

22
00:01:24.048 --> 00:01:26.444
Roxy yanked the clock's hand.

23
00:01:26.445 --> 00:01:33.575
She turned it to the present.

24
00:01:33.576 --> 00:01:38.460
Electricity shot through the lab.

25
00:01:38.461 --> 00:01:41.558
In a moment the electricity was gone.

26
00:01:41.559 --> 00:01:43.843
And so were the dinosaurs.

27
00:01:43.844 --> 00:01:47.950
Roxy took a deep breath. "Whew!"

28
00:01:47.951 --> 00:01:50.309
Professor Flashback grinned.

29
00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:52.970
"Thanks for saving my clock," he said.

30
00:01:52.971 --> 00:01:55.252
Roxy turned back to the clock.

31
00:01:55.253 --> 00:02:00.660
Whiz-hoo! Her eye laser beams blew the clock into a million pieces.

32
00:02:00.661 --> 00:02:04.608
"No!" the professor cried.

33
00:02:04.609 --> 00:02:07.709
"That clock is dangerous," said Roxy.

34
00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:11.875
"And you, Professor Flashback, are in big trouble."

35
00:02:11.876 --> 00:02:14.589
The professor narrowed his eyes at Roxy.

36
00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:16.548
He pulled his sleeve up.

37
00:02:16.549 --> 00:02:19.516
A small golden watch was on his wrist.

38
00:02:19.517 --> 00:02:23.225
"Good-bye, Rocket Girl," said Professor Flashback.

39
00:02:23.226 --> 00:02:26.233
He pressed a button on his watch.

40
00:02:26.234 --> 00:02:31.303
Za-wap! Electricity flashed and the professor disappeared!

41
00:02:31.304 --> 00:02:33.328
Roxy scratched her head.

42
00:02:33.329 --> 00:02:36.527
"I wonder where he went."

43
00:02:36.528 --> 00:02:40.482
The next day Roxy and her friends were at the Natural History Museum.

44
00:02:40.483 --> 00:02:43.701
Lots of fossils and dinosaur bones were on display.

45
00:02:43.702 --> 00:02:50.750
"Wow!" said Jack. "A T. rex skeleton!"

46
00:02:50.751 --> 00:02:56.408
Mara smiled. "It's a lot less scary than a live T. rex."

47
00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:58.725
Roxy pretended to sigh.

48
00:02:58.726 --> 00:03:02.701
"I can't believe I missed those dinosaurs."

49
00:03:02.702 --> 00:03:07.749
Terrell gave her a suspicious look.

50
00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:11.141
The friends saw a cave painting from the Stone Age.

51
00:03:11.142 --> 00:03:13.661
It showed cavemen hunting animals.

52
00:03:13.662 --> 00:03:16.889
One caveman looked different from the others.

53
00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:20.243
"Is that guy wearing a hat?" asked Terrell.

54
00:03:20.244 --> 00:03:22.618
"I think so," said Jack.

55
00:03:22.619 --> 00:03:26.034
"It looks like he has binoculars too."

56
00:03:26.035 --> 00:03:28.599
"That's weird," said Mara.

57
00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:31.640
"Binoculars didn't exist back then!"

58
00:03:31.641 --> 00:03:36.947
Roxy looked at the man and smiled.

59
00:03:36.948 --> 00:03:42.915
But she didn't say a word to her friends.
